From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 15:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] RedfishDiscoverDxe: skip the IPv6 discovery leg

The Redfish host interface is a point-to-point IPv4-static link (the
SMBIOS type 42 record carries static v4 addresses); RedfishDiscoverDxe
nevertheless builds a discover instance per entry of its protocol table,
running a second, IPv6 pass over the same NIC. That pass was in flight
(Ip6Dxe inside RedfishDiscoverDxe on the stack) during the 2026-08-17
use-after-free crash on a "BiosSetup" boot override, and at best it only
duplicates instances and REST EX children nothing consumes.

Note PcdIPv6HttpSupport does NOT gate this: in this tree that PCD is
consumed only by HttpBootDxe (HTTP boot option creation), despite
nuc-bios-build's 0020 setting it with Redfish intent.

Skip ProtocolTypeTcp6 when building network interfaces. The Tcp6 service
binding is still accepted by TestForRequiredProtocols(), so the platform
IPv6 stack, v6 PXE and v6 HTTP boot are untouched.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform policy]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/RedfishPkg/RedfishDiscoverDxe/RedfishDiscoverDxe.c
+++ b/RedfishPkg/RedfishDiscoverDxe/RedfishDiscoverDxe.c
@@ -1858,6 +1858,17 @@
   RestExInstance               = NULL;
 
   for (Index = 0; Index < ListCount; Index++) {
+    //
+    // RpiRedfish: skip the IPv6 leg. The Redfish host interface is a
+    // point-to-point IPv4-static link (SMBIOS type 42); a second discovery
+    // pass over Tcp6 only duplicates instances and REST EX children on the
+    // same NIC. Tcp6's presence is still accepted by
+    // TestForRequiredProtocols(), so platform IPv6 stays untouched.
+    //
+    if (mRequiredProtocol[Index].ProtocolType == ProtocolTypeTcp6) {
+      continue;
+    }
+
     Status = gBS->OpenProtocol (
                     // Already in list?
                     ControllerHandle,
